                "reply_count": 9,
                "retweet_count": 9,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "I just voted for the Lower Health Care Premiums for All Americans Act to give families and workers more affordable healthcare options.\n\u00a0\nObamacare did what we knew it would - increased costs and restricted choice. We\u00a0can\u2019t keep throwing your hard-earned tax dollars at insurance companies hoping that will fix everything. We need real reform.\n\u00a0\nThe Lower Health Care Premiums for All Americans Act does that by expanding health reimbursement arrangements (HRAs) and flexible spending accounts (FSAs), increasing transparency on pharmacy benefit managers, strengthening cost-sharing reductions, and giving folks more options through association health plans.\n\u00a0\nHealthcare costs have gotten totally out of control, and we\u2019ve got to do something to help all Americans, not just a select few.",
